      "writtenOn": "2022-12-23T10:37:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh there\u0027s both a sw option, an ITE driver and now a Zephyr API one. We could add SOC dependencies on what to build but in reality the Zephyr one should depend on `CONFIG_CRYPTO`, I think it\u0027s best to add a new option.\n\nSo how about:\n- add a new crypto backend choice in `zephyr/Kconfig` (PLATFORM_EC_SHA256_HW_ZEPHYR or something like that)\n- have that set as \"select CRYPTO\" (so we don\u0027t have to manually enable it, not completely sure it works in choices but let\u0027s try)\n- have that option as default for `PLATFORM_EC_SHA256_MODE` if `$(dt_nodelabel_enabled,cros_ec_sha)`\n- use the new option to build this driver\n\nI think that should take care of everything",
      "parentUuid": "a0f22627_c2a255e2",
      "revId": "26a981074770d07cf52e6b0401fcb60e130c914a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
